      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Can confirm this. I am working on a World for over 1 year now, I am getting to a state where I am finishing it. It started with a world size of around 90-110 MB, over the months, it accumulated, ofc, more data, and raised its overall Size to 160-205 MB. It fluctuates between those values, as I am compressing and changing stuff every time, to make things in terms of quality and usability excellent. I had a few times where I shoot temporarily over 200 MB just by a few up to 10-30 MB and it triggers this bug of uploading the world twice.\n\nThere is only this one error, and nothing else so far.\n\nThis has been an issue for over 8 months now (ever since I had this noticed while uploading a world size over 200 MB the first time).\n\nReducing the size down to 199.99 MB or more gets rid off that issue.\n\nCurrent used SDK versions, World & Base: 3.10.5\n\nOh, and more Info added to this: The progress bar fills up to around 5/6, when the status reaches 100% the first time (instead of fully filling it up), starts the upload process again from anew and continues on filling that bar to its full size.\n\nMy world is currently only PC-compatible, so no Android or iOS is being selected (Multi-Platform-Upload) during my upload.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
